  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nAs high pressure continues to drift eastward thru Thu, southwest\nwinds will gradually increase. This will be most pronounced by\nafternoon, where winds may be breezy and temps will climb well\ninto the 60s and maybe even hit 70 in a few spots. The cold\nfront will not cross the area until Fri, so Thu night will be\nquite mild for this time of year and especially mild compared to\nrecent min temps. Some locations are unlikely to drop out of the\n50s, which will be within a few degrees of the record warm min\ntemps for this time of year.\n\nThe frontal passage itself looks to be mostly dry again, but a\nstray shower or sprinkle remains possible. This will be most\nlikely where upslope winds helping with lifting north of the\nmtns. \n\nAfter the front we return to dry and seasonable weather. Temps\nare expected to be near normal for Halloween, with most areas\nstarting the trick or treating in the 40s and 50s, falling into\nthe 30s by the time the candy bowls are empty. Ensembles\ncontinue to show a flip to a wetter weather pattern to start \nNovember, but they also continue to push this back in time so\nthere is plenty of time for that to change.",
